title: What a day in Vietnam actually costs — the full breakdown
format: guide
voice: af_heart
music: upbeat
score: upbeat@1 cafe@6 upbeat@10 emotional@19 cafe@24 upbeat@28
sources: vietadvisor.travel daily costs 2026; jackfruitadventure Hanoi street food (Apr 2026); daytripsvietnam cost index 2026 (rate 26,025 ₫/USD; motorbike rental 100–250k ₫/day; Grab car 50–120k ₫); asiatouradvisor Hà Giang homestays ($6–15). All checked Oct 2026.
// YOUTUBE CUT (16:9): one continuous day, no chapters — dawn to night carries the structure; the airport rule, the costs nobody lists, three budgets ride inside the flow.
// Each new time of day opens on a wide street move (the light tells the viewer where we are). Re-hook every 60–90 s with a number or a question.
// 0:00 HOOK — dawn, the street rises into frame, "$17?" on the first word.
# nw focus=cafe cam=rise time=dawn head="$17?|one full day in Vietnam" dur=5
Guess what one full day in Vietnam costs.
Breakfast. Coffee. Rides. Two meals, a beer, and a bed.
// 0:08 promise montage — the day in objects.
# vis kind=daycycle trans=blobs stops="06:30:banhmi:Breakfast|09:00:caphe_phin:Coffee|12:00:pho:Lunch|19:00:biahoi:Evening|22:00:backpack:Bed" sub="every price, checked this month"
In the next five minutes: every price from one ordinary day.
Three budgets, from backpacker to comfortable.
And the one habit that quietly makes everything cost four times more.
// CH.1 MORNING
# nw focus=cart cam=truck time=dawn trans=whip head="6:30 AM|the street wakes up"
It starts at six thirty, when the street wakes up.
# nw focus=cart cam=push zoom=1.4 time=dawn trans=zoomthru tc=.3,.6 tags="cart:25.000 ₫:≈ $1:1.0"
Breakfast is a bánh mì from a cart. Twenty-five thousand dong.
# vis kind=build set=banhmi trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.52 parts="pate:PÂTÉ|pork:GRILLED PORK|pickles:PICKLED CARROT|cucumber:CUCUMBER|herbs:CORIANDER|chili:CHILI|sauce:MAGGI" sub="inside a 25k bánh mì" final="25.000 ₫|about one dollar"
Here's what one dollar buys:
pâté,
grilled pork,
pickled carrot,
cucumber,
coriander,
chili,
and Maggi.
# vis kind=vs bg=teal trans=slices a=banhmi an="CART" pa=25000 b=banhmi bn="AIR-CON CAFÉ" pb=55000 win=a head="SAME SANDWICH" verdict="2× MORE|for the air-con"
The same sandwich inside a café with air conditioning? Fifty to sixty thousand.
# vis kind=coffee bg=wine trans=liquid tcol=#6a3a1e head="20.000 ₫|iced coffee on a stool" price="20.000 ₫" sub="≈ $0.80"
Iced black coffee on a plastic stool: twenty thousand.
A specialty café charges fifty to ninety for the same beans.
// CH.2 GETTING AROUND
# nw focus=cafe cam=truckL time=day trans=stripes2 head="9:00 AM|time to move"
Then you need to get across town.
# vis kind=ride bg=sea trans=whip head="30.000 ₫|GrabBike across the centre" price="30.000 ₫"
A GrabBike across the centre is twenty to fifty thousand. Call it thirty.
A car for the same trip: fifty to a hundred and twenty.
# vis kind=bars bg=night trans=cube items="In the app:240000:phone|First kerb price:480000:suitcase" hi=1 unit=" ₫" head="THE AIRPORT RULE|first kerb price ≈ double"
The airport is where most people lose money on day one.
In the app, airport to the centre runs two hundred to two hundred and eighty thousand.
At the kerb, the first price is usually double.
// CH.3 MIDDAY
# nw focus=pho cam=drift zoom=1.5 time=day trans=ripple tc=.5,.5 head="NOON|the lunch rush"
By noon, the lunch rush is on.
# vis kind=build set=pho bg=ember trans=zoomthru tc=.4,.55 parts="broth:BROTH|noodles:RICE NOODLES|beef:RARE BEEF|herbs:HERBS|lime:LIME" sub="a 45k bowl" final="45.000 ₫|40–55k in Hà Nội"
Lunch is phở. Broth simmered all night,
rice noodles,
rare beef that cooks in the bowl,
herbs,
and lime. Forty to fifty-five thousand in Hà Nội.
# vis kind=receipt bg=teal trans=burst items="banhmi:Bánh mì:25000|caphe_phin:Cà phê:20000|scooter:GrabBike:30000|pho:Phở:45000" final="120.000 ₫|spent by noon · ≈ $4.60" sub="spent so far"
Bánh mì.
Coffee.
A ride.
Phở.
By noon you've spent a hundred and twenty thousand. Four dollars sixty.
# vis kind=ticket bg=plum trans=cube head="40.000 ₫|most museums" price="40.000 ₫"
Most museums cost forty thousand. A viewing deck is two hundred.
// CH.4 NIGHT
# nw focus=biahoi cam=push zoom=1.35 time=night trans=bloom tc=.5,.3 tcol=#ffd98a head="7:00 PM|the lanterns come on"
At seven, the lanterns come on.
# vis kind=cheers bg=indigo trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.6
Bia hơi is brewed in the morning and gone by night. Seven to fifteen thousand a glass.
Two glasses still costs less than half a dollar.
# vis kind=build set=buncha bg=ember trans=match tc=.5,.55 tc2=.5,.62 parts="patties:GRILLED PATTIES|pork:PORK BELLY|papaya:PICKLED PAPAYA|noodles:NOODLES|herbs:HERBS" sub="bún chả over coals" final="55.000 ₫|45–65k"
Dinner is bún chả, grilled over coals.
Patties,
pork belly,
pickled papaya,
noodles,
herbs. Forty-five to sixty-five thousand.
// CH.5 THE BED
# vis kind=bed bg=night trans=drop head="200.000 ₫|a dorm bed" price="200.000 ₫" sub="dorm · ≈ $8"
Then you need a bed. A dorm bed is a hundred to three hundred thousand.
# vis kind=vs bg=night trans=slices a=backpack an="DORM BED" pa=200000 b=suitcase bn="3-STAR HOTEL" pb=750000 win=a head="PER NIGHT" verdict="FROM 750.000 ₫|for a 3-star"
A private room starts around three hundred. A three-star hotel runs seven hundred and fifty thousand upward.
# vis kind=hagiang trans=spin head="155.000 ₫|a homestay in Hà Giang" price="155.000 ₫" sub="dinner included"
And those are city prices.
Up in Hà Giang, a homestay bed is about a hundred and fifty-five thousand. Dinner usually comes with it.
// CH.6 COSTS NOBODY LISTS
# vis kind=grid bg=sea trans=blobs items="sim:SIM · 100–300k / month|moto:Motorbike · 100–250k / day|sleeperbus:Sleeper bus · $15–25|plane:Flight · $40–80" head="ONCE, NOT DAILY|costs nobody lists"
But a trip has costs nobody puts in a daily budget.
A local SIM: a hundred to three hundred thousand for a month of data.
A motorbike: a hundred to two hundred and fifty thousand a day.
An overnight sleeper bus: fifteen to twenty-five dollars, and it saves a hotel night.
A domestic flight booked three weeks ahead: forty to eighty dollars.
// PAYOFF
# vis kind=receipt trans=burst bg=night items="banhmi:Bánh mì:25000|caphe_phin:Cà phê:20000|scooter:GrabBike:30000|pho:Phở:45000|ticket:Museum:40000|biahoi:Bia hơi ×2:20000|buncha:Bún chả:55000|backpack:Dorm bed:200000" final="435.000 ₫|≈ $17 for the whole day"
Back to the day. Add the eight prices up.
Bánh mì, coffee, a ride, phở,
a museum, two beers, bún chả, a bed.
Four hundred and thirty-five thousand dong. About seventeen dollars.
// THE TRAP
# nw focus=hotel cam=push time=day trans=stripes2 head="THE TRAP|two price lists" tags="hotel:90.000 ₫:same coffee:1.4"
Now the habit that breaks the budget.
Vietnam has two price lists, and nobody tells you which one you're reading.
# vis kind=vs bg=teal trans=match a=caphe_phin an="STREET STOOL" pa=20000 b=caphe_suada bn="HOTEL LOBBY" pb=90000 win=a head="SAME COFFEE" verdict="4.5× MORE|for the chair"
The same iced coffee, fifty metres apart.
Twenty thousand… or ninety.
Nobody is cheating you. You're just standing in the wrong queue.
// BUDGETS
# vis kind=bars bg=indigo trans=cube items="Backpacker:13|Comfortable:35|Easy:95" hi=1 pre="$" head="3 BUDGETS|per person, per day"
So, three budgets. Thirteen dollars with dorms and street food.
Thirty-five with a private room and a sit-down dinner.
Ninety-five if you want a pool and taxis everywhere.
// RULES
# vis kind=grid trans=blobs items="stool:Eat where stools are full|money:Agree the price first|phone:Book rides in the app|!caphe_suada:Skip lobby cafés" head="SAVE THIS|before your trip"
Three rules, and they're the whole video.
Eat where the plastic stools are already full.
Agree a price before you get on anything.
Book rides in the app, not at the kerb.
# vis kind=trainstreet trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.5 head="NEXT|Train Street"
Seventeen dollars, for a day most people remember for years.
Next time: the most filmed street in Hà Nội, and why sitting on it is against the rules.
